 "observation": "Ten real dynamic-loader arms were executed twice, once against the pinned head 29595023021c1f1d6bc6b1e75307301a34bd0cd6 and once against the pinned base ae3077a09f2dcc7970721f7d06c6022de49ced1f, for both launchers (llama-server and whisper-server). In every arm the product's own child-env builder produced the environment, a real process was spawned with it and its environment was read back from that child's /proc/<pid>/environ, and CUDA resolution was performed by the real glibc loader /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 running a compiled ELF whose NEEDED entries are the exact SONAMEs libcudart.so.13 and libcublas.so.13. The vendored cudart/cublas files are byte-identical copies of the host toolkit's CUDA 13 payloads (sha256 matched), and each arm's resolved object path was read back from the loader child's own /proc/<pid>/maps.\n\nHEAD: on the unpatched host (ldconfig readable, its cache naming a system CUDA 13) both launchers withheld the vendored dir and the child mapped the system /usr/local/cuda-13.1 payloads. With the cache unreadable (real RLIMIT_NPROC=0 blocked exec) both launchers appended the vendored dir last and the child mapped both CUDA objects from the vendored dir (rc 0); the same binary with the appended dir removed failed rc 127. The exact-SONAME vendored shape loads when forced (rc 0), and the payload-only shape (fully-versioned filenames, no SONAME entry) fails rc 127 while the helper refuses that dir. In the synthetic arch-dir sub-arms, an unreadable cache with the arch dir populated yielded 'already provides' and a withhold, while the same dir emptied yielded 'not provided', an append, and a vendored resolution.\n\nBASE: it never appends any vendored dir in any arm, so every unreadable-cache arm fails rc 127 for both launchers, while its host-default and system-precedence arms do resolve the system objects. The base/head difference is therefore exactly the append the change introduces, with the withhold behaviour preserved.",
